OL,3,AFamily blame police for 'Putney pusher'
OL,4,Asuspect's death
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe family of Nicholas Brandram have
OL,7,Finsisted he was not the so-called
OL,8,F"Putney pusher" and have blamed the
OL,9,FMetropolitan Police for his death.
OL,11,FThe 44-year-old was under suspicion of
OL,12,Fbeing the jogger who pushed a woman
OL,13,Finto the path of a bus during a run on
OL,14,FPutney Bridge in west London in May
OL,15,F2017.
OL,17,FBrandram's family said he "took his own
OL,18,Flife after months of immense pressure
OL,19,Fcaused by a Metropolitan Police
OL,20,Finvestigation" and there was no
OL,21,Fforensic evidence linking the banker to
OL,22,Fthe incident.
OL,23,APub: 17-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
